      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4f96a9d5-431b-5a23-aab8-fc03e5905952",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris DeStefano, Brett Eldredge, Carrie Underwood, Billy Currington, Luke Bryan, Miranda Lambert, Jason Aldean, Terry Eldredge\n- Organizations: The Grascals, Billboard, NBC Sunday Night Football\n- Places: Mt. Laurel, New Jersey, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Songs: Good Girl, Little Toy Guns, Hey Girl, Don't Ya, That's My Kind of Night, Kick the Dust Up, Somethin' Bad, Rewind, Just Gettin' Started, Beat of the Music, Mean to Me, Drunk on Your Love\n- Albums: Bring You Back\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, record producer, multi-instrumentalist\n\nFacts:\n- Chris DeStefano is an American singer-songwriter, record producer, and multi-instrumentalist who was raised in Mt. Laurel, New Jersey and lives in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- Chris DeStefano is a Grammy Award-winning songwriter with multiple No. 1 songs, including \"Good Girl\" and \"Little Toy Guns\" for Carrie Underwood, \"Hey Girl\" for Billy Currington, \"Don't Ya\" for Brett Eldredge, \"That's My Kind of Night\" and \"Kick the Dust Up\" for Luke Bryan, \"Somethin' Bad\" for Miranda Lambert and Carrie Underwood, \"Rewind\" for Rascal Flatts, and \"Just Gettin' Started\" for Jason Aldean.\n- Chris DeStefano's song \"Somethin' Bad\" was later reworked as the opening theme for NBC Sunday Night Football.\n- Brett Eldredge is the cousin of Terry Eldredge of The Grascals.\n- Brett Eldredge had three No. 1 singles on the Billboard Country Airplay chart from his debut studio album \"Bring You Back\": \"Don't Ya,\" \"Beat of the Music,\" and \"Mean to Me.\"\n- \"Drunk on Your Love\" is a song that Brett Eldredge co-wrote and recorded.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3336f52f-cbc5-5799-9a3b-bdbdda004a38",
        "text": "Page: Chris DeStefano. Sentence: Christopher Michael \"Chris\" DeStefano is a Grammy Award Winning American singer/songwriter, record producer and multi instrumentalist, raised in Mt. Laurel, New Jersey and currently residing in Nashville, Tennessee.\nPage: Chris DeStefano. Sentence: As a songwriter, he has multiple #1 songs with artists Carrie Underwood (“Good Girl”, \"Little Toy Guns\"), Billy Currington (“Hey Girl”), Brett Eldredge (\"Don't Ya\"), Luke Bryan (\"That's My Kind of Night\", \"Kick the Dust Up\" ), Miranda Lambert & Carrie Underwood (\"Somethin' Bad,\" later reworked as the opening theme for \"NBC Sunday Night Football\"), Rascal Flatts (\"Rewind\") and Jason Aldean (\"Just Gettin' Started\").\nPage: Brett Eldredge. Sentence: The cousin of Terry Eldredge of The Grascals, Eldredge has had three No. 1 singles on the \"Billboard\" Country Airplay chart from his debut studio album, \"Bring You Back\": \"Don't Ya\", \"Beat of the Music\", and \"Mean to Me\".\nPage: Drunk on Your Love. Sentence: \"Drunk on Your Love\" is a song co-written and recorded by American country music artist Brett Eldredge.",
